# Initial multicopter vertical tuning for the 1560 kg Mk-7 model.
# Hover thrust: the hover-thrust estimator converged to ~0.50 in SITL (WK01 run 6), consistent with 0.49.
# Gazebo MulticopterMotorModel (velocity): thrust = k*omega^2 with omega linear in the command, i.e. quadratic
# thrust. THR_MDL_FAC was the default 0 (linear) -> hover cmd 0.70 was really 49 % thrust, and the transition
# lift-handoff floor delivered only (cmd)^2 of the intended rotor lift (sink before/after FW entry, runs 2-5).
# Real rotors are also ~quadratic. MC rate P/D scaled x1.4 (= d thrust/d cmd at hover, 2*0.70) to keep the
# loop gain that was tuned with the linear model.
